{"seconds": 53.3, "exit": 0, "final": "After Re7 Qg1+, White plays Kxg1 and the queen is captured. So the pattern is clear: **Re7 wins because it threatens Rxf7 and forces Black's queen to give checks that allow White to capture it.**\n\nMain line: **1. Re7 Qf3+ (or Qe1+ or Qg1+) 2. Qxf3** (or Rexe1 or Kxg1)\n\n```json\n{\"move\": \"Re7\", \"line\": [\"Re7\", \"Qf3+\", \"Qxf3\", \"Rd8\", \"Rxf7\", \"Kg8\"], \"motifs\": [\"quietMove\", \"attraction\"]}\n```\n\n**Coaching Note:**\n\nLook for quiet moves that create **unstoppable threats**, not just forcing checks. Here, Re7 quietly attacks f7 and threatens Rxf7+. Black's queen must leave f2 to give checks (Qf3+, Qe1+, Qg1+), but then each check allows White to capture it\u2014Qxf3, Rexe1, or Kxg1. The lesson: when your opponent's queen is active but the pieces it guards are pinned or trapped, a quiet threat forcing them to move first often wins material.", "tool_calls": [{"tool": "skill", "args": {"skill": "chess-coach"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-board", "args": {"fen": "3r1r2/pp3bpk/2p5/4R3/6Q1/1P4P1/PB3q1P/R6K w - - 1 24"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-threats", "args": {"fen": "3r1r2/pp3bpk/2p5/4R3/6Q1/1P4P1/PB3q1P/R6K w - - 1 24"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "3r1r2/pp3bpk/2p5/4R3/6Q1/1P4P1/PB3q1P/R6K w - - 1 24", "move": "Rxf7"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "3r1r2/pp3bpk/2p5/4R3/6Q1/1P4P1/PB3q1P/R6K w - - 1 24", "move": "Re7"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "3r1r2/pp3bpk/2p5/4R3/6Q1/1P4P1/PB3q1P/R6K w - - 1 24", "move": "Qd7"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "3r1r2/pp3bpk/2p5/4R3/6Q1/1P4P1/PB3q1P/R6K w - - 1 24", "move": "Qe4"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "3r1r2/pp3bpk/2p5/4R3/6Q1/1P4P1/PB3q1P/R6K w - - 1 24", "move": "Re6"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "3r1r2/pp3bpk/2p5/4R3/6Q1/1P4P1/PB3q1P/R6K w - - 1 24", "move": "Qe2"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "3r